    "node-1md6ssy": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims the briefing 'listed topic... with no valve-by-valve content' and that it did not document specific isolation steps. The evidence (IA-S02) confirms the daily work briefing was issued on 2024-05-20 but does not contain a transcript or summary of its spoken/typed content beyond the title '1SC dryer work and RHOB service coordination'. While IA-D03 requires an ECP revision for boundary changes, it does not mandate that every daily briefing must list valve-by-valve isolation steps. The node's detail asserts a negative fact ('did not document specific isolation steps') which cannot be proven solely because the supplied excerpt lacks the full text of the briefing; absence in this packet is unknown status.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Full content or summary of the Daily work briefing (2024-05-20) to verify whether it contained valve-by-valve isolation steps, specific boundary integrity checks, or if those details were omitted. Alternatively, a record confirming that such detail is not required for this type of assignment.",
      "question": "Does the full Daily work briefing (IA-S02 attachment 'Daily work briefing') contain specific isolation steps and boundary verification instructions beyond its title?"
    },
    "node-1ji7zuu": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims the event was treated as an unplanned deviation requiring investigation before resumption. The evidence (IA-S01) states at 10:20 'Maintenance deferred' and 'Work folder retained for review'. This supports that work stopped and a record was kept. However, it does not explicitly state that an *investigation* occurred or is required by policy; the node's detail infers this requirement from the deferral action without citing a specific rule (e.g., IA-D03 Section 5.1 mentions initial notification before event sequence check but doesn't mandate investigation for all interruptions). The claim of 'requiring investigation' is an interpretation not fully supported by the text.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A policy excerpt or procedure stating that maintenance deferral due to air loss requires a formal investigation, OR evidence (interview log, report) showing such an investigation was initiated after 10:20.",
      "question": "Is there a documented requirement in IA-D03 or another record that mandates an RCA-style investigation whenever work is deferred due to instrument-air interruption?"
    },
    "node-1o9by9l": {
